A||||6||Cheever2||Battery drain or not charge (voltage light on)||||2||
Z||000000||Cheever2||07-25-2001||01:17 AM||||On the way to work this afternoon, my VOLTS light is on.  The needle is at about the "10".  Everything seemed to work normal.  Coming home just now the lights were dim, the turn signals were very slow, and the power window almost didn't go all the way up.  I have to drive it in the morning, so I put the battery charger on it, and it pegged out.  This is my 88 GT with 2.8, all stock, 64000 miles, manual, with an almost brand new NAPA Orbital battery.  This is the car I had to get a new positive cable side-post connector a few days ago.<P>What can I do myself, in order to avoid shop costs?  TIA<P><P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||2
Z||000001||saleenfiero||07-25-2001||01:44 AM||||Exact same symptoms happened to me, was my alt failing||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cheever2||07-25-2001||07:34 AM||||That's what I was thinking.<P>I wonder if this is a result of driving through the deep water in the Allison flood.<P>Guess I'll let the shop check it out after all.  Thanks.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||maryjane||07-25-2001||07:39 AM||||Yep, alternator. has all the symptoms. A bad battery or bad connecttion makes alt work harder=shortened life. 'doubt those cool Hou area days have anything to do with it'  good luck- around $100 for a good one for my 84<BR>Don||||reg||1
Z||000004||Cheever2||07-25-2001||04:48 PM||||Great... looks like I'll have to postpone swapping my rear bumper ANOTHER week.  I just hope Expeditor will hold up for me two more days.<P>I'm sitting here reading the Forum while in an IBM class my company paid $1700 for!  Woo-hoo!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever2||07-27-2001||08:25 AM||||Very strange: <BR>The next day, the Voltage light was off, and apparently the battery is once again being charged.  Everything seems fine again... <BR>...except...<BR>now I have a whining sound from the engine area.  It increases in pitch as the RPM's go up.  It's not the belt squealing.  Guess I should still plan on replacing the alternator, huh?  It's easy to do myself, right?<P><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 07-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||elfiero||07-27-2001||08:29 AM||||Sounds like one of the diodes in the alt.<BR>is failing-this is very common.just go get a<BR>rebuilt alternator and the problem will be<BR>solved!||||reg||6
